1
00:00:14,529 --> 00:00:18,368
<i>SAWYER FARM
ESTABLISHED 1845

2
00:00:19,994 --> 00:00:29,048
<i># Happy birthday to you...

3
00:00:29,172 --> 00:00:34,013
<i># Happy birthday, dear Jed...

4
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:38,934
<i># Happy birthday to you...

5
00:00:39,059 --> 00:00:40,771
All right, now make a wish.

6
00:00:40,806 --> 00:00:41,773
Blow them out.

7
00:00:46,568 --> 00:00:48,821
Yes! Very good!

8
00:00:48,862 --> 00:00:51,032
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

9
00:00:51,073 --> 00:00:52,284
Very good!

10
00:00:52,408 --> 00:00:53,702
All right...

11
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,586
Drayton, where are your manners?

12
00:00:59,669 --> 00:01:01,838
Give the first slice to the thief.

13
00:01:16,605 --> 00:01:18,086
I didn't steal your damn pigs...

14
00:01:18,121 --> 00:01:19,568
Are you calling my son a liar?

15
00:01:19,693 --> 00:01:21,946
He saw your filthy hands stealing our property...

16
00:01:26,532 --> 00:01:29,329
Why would I go anywhere near your filthy pigs?

17
00:01:29,453 --> 00:01:30,915
Or your filthy family!

18
00:01:30,998 --> 00:01:34,085
I swear, everybody will know what kind of...

19
00:01:34,126 --> 00:01:36,004
...offspring you're raising here, Verna!

20
00:01:36,086 --> 00:01:37,923
Shut him up! I've had enough!

21
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,433
Listen to me, no farmhand is going to...

22
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:43,264
...ruin my son's special night.

23
00:01:46,517 --> 00:01:47,894
Ready for your present?

24
00:01:51,189 --> 00:01:53,192
You know you're my special boy.

25
00:01:53,775 --> 00:01:55,862
Come on, Jed. There you go...

26
00:01:58,699 --> 00:02:00,952
- Jed.
- Yes, that's it, Jed.

27
00:02:03,455 --> 00:02:04,499
Now remember,

28
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:07,836
bad people like him try to destroy our family.

29
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:10,256
But we won't let that happen, will we?

30
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:11,798
Go on, pick it up...

31
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:14,093
Jed, pick it up...

32
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:15,470
Jed!

33
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:19,223
Jed...

34
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:20,810
Pick it up, Jed!

35
00:02:20,851 --> 00:02:24,147
Jed!

36
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:26,941
Come on, you know what you have to do...

37
00:02:27,358 --> 00:02:29,071
That's it, Jed!

38
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,491
Come on, Jed...

39
00:02:33,199 --> 00:02:36,037
Jed!

40
00:02:36,119 --> 00:02:37,580
No!

41
00:02:37,621 --> 00:02:38,874
There you go.

42
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:40,542
Go on, son!

43
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:41,878
No!

44
00:02:48,592 --> 00:02:50,304
No!

45
00:02:55,894 --> 00:02:57,981
No!

46
00:02:58,147 --> 00:02:59,983
No, please!

47
00:03:00,108 --> 00:03:02,903
No!

48
00:03:02,944 --> 00:03:05,573
Do it, do it, do it!

49
00:03:05,614 --> 00:03:07,575
No!

50
00:03:07,616 --> 00:03:09,327
Go on, Jed, do it...

51
00:03:10,286 --> 00:03:11,330
Do it!

52
00:03:11,914 --> 00:03:14,126
- Jed.
- Do it!

53
00:03:20,423 --> 00:03:21,551
Mom!

54
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,594
Mom, no!

55
00:03:25,346 --> 00:03:28,685
No!

56
00:03:38,571 --> 00:03:39,406
Hey.

57
00:03:39,697 --> 00:03:41,284
You let us down, Jed.

58
00:03:44,036 --> 00:03:47,123
It's all right. Family will always be here for
you.

59
00:03:47,289 --> 00:03:48,624
Remember that.

60
00:03:49,375 --> 00:03:50,418
All right.

61
00:04:08,106 --> 00:04:13,197
<i>TEXAS, 1955

62
00:04:16,198 --> 00:04:17,619
Are you trying to get us killed?

63
00:04:17,659 --> 00:04:18,536
Do you want me to stop?

64
00:04:18,578 --> 00:04:19,829
No, I didn't say that.

65
00:04:27,130 --> 00:04:28,216
Watch out!

66
00:04:32,929 --> 00:04:34,725
What the hell was that thing?

67
00:04:36,016 --> 00:04:37,228
Hey, Betty.

68
00:04:44,443 --> 00:04:45,695
What is it?

69
00:04:46,987 --> 00:04:48,115
I don't know.

70
00:04:51,368 --> 00:04:52,830
Then let's go.

71
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,092
What?

72
00:05:11,476 --> 00:05:12,812
He's just a kid!

73
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:16,150
Let's go!

74
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:17,943
We'll be late.

75
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:21,572
Hello.

76
00:05:25,828 --> 00:05:27,122
Are you okay?

77
00:05:33,253 --> 00:05:35,298
You shouldn't play in the road.

78
00:05:35,464 --> 00:05:37,425
Help me, please...

79
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,561
Hey, Betty, where are you going? I didn't hit him!

80
00:05:45,977 --> 00:05:47,605
- Something's wrong.
- Betty!

81
00:05:47,645 --> 00:05:49,065
He needs help.

82
00:05:49,607 --> 00:05:51,025
Jesus Christ!

83
00:05:55,447 --> 00:05:57,409
Hey, buddy, can you hear me?

84
00:05:59,411 --> 00:06:00,954
Let me help you!

85
00:06:04,832 --> 00:06:06,001
Hello?

86
00:06:12,633 --> 00:06:15,222
It's okay. You can come out.

87
00:06:16,679 --> 00:06:17,808
Betty.

88
00:06:21,603 --> 00:06:23,314
Betty, where did you go?

89
00:07:21,594 --> 00:07:22,889
Hello?

90
00:07:28,061 --> 00:07:31,607
Come on... I won't hurt you.

91
00:07:34,150 --> 00:07:35,653
I just want to help...

92
00:07:42,703 --> 00:07:43,872
Okay?

93
00:07:54,761 --> 00:07:59,058
<i>BASED ON CHARACTERS CREATED BY

94
00:07:59,140 --> 00:08:02,104
<i>KIM HENKEL AND TOBE HOOPER

95
00:08:04,397 --> 00:08:06,441
You did good, Jed!

96
00:08:07,233 --> 00:08:10,279
It's like... I can still feel you in there
after all.

97
00:08:41,607 --> 00:08:45,196
Well, let him learn a little more.

98
00:08:48,657 --> 00:08:50,202
Oh, my God!

99
00:08:59,838 --> 00:09:00,757
Show him!

100
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:15,357
- Where is she?
- Calm down, Hal.

101
00:09:15,857 --> 00:09:17,444
Let me through, damn it!

102
00:09:17,485 --> 00:09:19,030
Let me go! Let me go, damn it!

103
00:09:19,070 --> 00:09:20,655
- We know what happened.
- Calm down, Hal.

104
00:09:20,821 --> 00:09:22,450
Is that my little girl in there?

105
00:09:23,951 --> 00:09:26,830
Is she in there? Is my little girl in there?

106
00:09:27,164 --> 00:09:28,541
Answer me, damn it!

107
00:09:28,874 --> 00:09:30,251
We've got one of them.

108
00:09:34,630 --> 00:09:36,009
Oh, boy!

109
00:09:40,179 --> 00:09:41,557
I couldn't get to her in time!

110
00:09:41,765 --> 00:09:43,810
I'm so sorry, sir. I swear to God.

111
00:09:46,311 --> 00:09:48,022
Drayton Sawyer...

112
00:09:50,524 --> 00:09:52,403
It's time to go to Gorman Reformatory.

113
00:09:52,444 --> 00:09:55,783
No... You're all grown up now.

114
00:09:58,034 --> 00:10:00,038
That means the gas chamber for you.

115
00:10:03,708 --> 00:10:04,962
Why?

116
00:10:05,294 --> 00:10:07,131
Are you going to arrest me for finding a dead
body?

117
00:10:07,338 --> 00:10:08,800
Last I checked, that wasn't a crime.

118
00:10:08,849 --> 00:10:11,603
How about a bullet hole in your damn skull?

119
00:10:12,269 --> 00:10:13,569
- Put it away, Hal.
- Come on.

120
00:10:13,604 --> 00:10:15,482
He's right. We've got nothing on him...

121
00:10:15,856 --> 00:10:17,065
Calm down, Hal.

122
00:10:17,273 --> 00:10:18,025
Keep your head clear.

123
00:10:18,065 --> 00:10:20,569
- Hal, it's not worth it.
- Come on, Hal, lower the gun.

124
00:10:20,693 --> 00:10:22,029
Damn trash.

125
00:10:33,205 --> 00:10:35,166
Let those boys go right this instant!

126
00:10:35,457 --> 00:10:37,126
Don't count on it, Verna!

127
00:10:37,876 --> 00:10:39,337
Do you think they did anything wrong?

128
00:10:39,377 --> 00:10:40,463
No, I don't!

129
00:10:40,545 --> 00:10:42,381
You bastard, let them out of the car!

130
00:10:42,881 --> 00:10:45,676
No! They're going to stay there and rot!

131
00:10:46,759 --> 00:10:47,844
On what charges?

132
00:10:48,135 --> 00:10:49,429
They're not under arrest.

133
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:51,765
They're in protective custody... from you.

134
00:10:51,806 --> 00:10:53,058
What are you talking about?

135
00:10:54,058 --> 00:10:56,603
I can't count how many crime scenes I've been
to...

136
00:10:56,644 --> 00:10:58,981
...where there's always a Sawyer involved.

137
00:10:59,523 --> 00:11:01,316
Those boys aren't safe with you...

138
00:11:01,398 --> 00:11:02,526
Bullshit.

139
00:11:03,442 --> 00:11:05,780
Get a warrant for the Sawyer house.

140
00:11:06,112 --> 00:11:08,157
Name every one of them. I want them all.

141
00:11:08,323 --> 00:11:09,325
- Did you hear me?
- You can't do that.

142
00:11:09,407 --> 00:11:10,284
You can't do that!

143
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:12,078
Well, by the time we get there, I'll have a
warrant saying I can...

144
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,621
...do just that.

145
00:11:14,287 --> 00:11:16,414
It's called "children at risk."

146
00:11:17,832 --> 00:11:19,793
You took one of mine...

147
00:11:20,543 --> 00:11:22,963
...so I'll take every one of yours, Verna.

148
00:11:29,135 --> 00:11:30,511
Every last one of them...

149
00:11:32,513 --> 00:11:34,516
<i>10 YEARS LATER

150
00:11:34,974 --> 00:11:38,645
<i>In 1935, the state of Texas established a...

151
00:11:38,686 --> 00:11:41,189
<i>...program to care for children at risk.

152
00:11:41,355 --> 00:11:44,693
In its first year, nearly 52 children were
removed from homes...

153
00:11:44,774 --> 00:11:47,611
...known to be involved in criminal activity.

154
00:11:47,944 --> 00:11:50,824
<i>Many of these children were given new names...

155
00:11:50,865 --> 00:11:52,659
<i>...and placed in foster homes.

156
00:11:52,783 --> 00:11:56,371
<i>Others, products of degenerate parenting...

157
00:11:56,412 --> 00:11:59,249
<i>...ended up here at Gorman Reformatory.

158
00:11:59,290 --> 00:12:00,665
<i>GORMAN HOUSE JUVENILE REFORMATORY

159
00:12:00,706 --> 00:12:04,836
We take care of their physical and
psychological needs.

160
00:12:05,294 --> 00:12:06,547
Yes, sir.

161
00:12:06,671 --> 00:12:09,467
I've wanted to come here for a long time.

162
00:12:09,757 --> 00:12:11,093
I think I can help them.

163
00:12:11,259 --> 00:12:12,303
Elizabeth.

164
00:12:12,343 --> 00:12:13,971
Please, sir, Lizzy. Lizzy is fine.

165
00:12:14,012 --> 00:12:15,513
Elizabeth.

166
00:12:16,472 --> 00:12:18,725
Most of these children will end up...

167
00:12:18,765 --> 00:12:20,977
...in prisons or mental institutions.

168
00:12:22,019 --> 00:12:25,483
Keeping them here makes everyone safer.

169
00:12:26,274 --> 00:12:27,526
Keep your guard up.

170
00:13:12,194 --> 00:13:13,571
Well... hello...

171
00:13:14,404 --> 00:13:15,865
My name is Lizzy.

172
00:13:15,948 --> 00:13:18,827
I'm new here, and I'd like to get to know you.

173
00:13:23,372 --> 00:13:24,707
That's Bud.

174
00:13:26,333 --> 00:13:28,709
He doesn't say much for such a big guy.

175
00:13:34,132 --> 00:13:35,134
You're in my seat.

176
00:13:35,675 --> 00:13:36,844
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:37,718 --> 00:13:39,721
- Very nice.
- I'm...

178
00:13:39,762 --> 00:13:41,807
Lizzy... Yeah, I heard. I heard.

179
00:13:42,806 --> 00:13:44,976
Shit, sorry. I'm Jackson.

180
00:13:45,767 --> 00:13:48,730
Jackson and... Bud...

181
00:13:49,522 --> 00:13:51,984
And what medication are you taking, Jackson?

182
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:53,360
Medication?

183
00:13:54,569 --> 00:13:56,530
They already gave it to us when they brought
us in, right?

184
00:13:57,529 --> 00:14:00,449
We figured you'd know more about that than we
do, Lizzy...

185
00:14:01,449 --> 00:14:03,871
You're not going to give me any trouble, are you?

186
00:14:04,370 --> 00:14:05,831
No, not me, Lizzy.

187
00:14:07,165 --> 00:14:08,464
Is there a reason you keep...

188
00:14:08,499 --> 00:14:10,043
...saying my name like that?

189
00:14:10,626 --> 00:14:14,880
No... I just like to know who's in charge,
that's all.

190
00:14:17,965 --> 00:14:19,635
Fuck you, asshole!

191
00:14:19,676 --> 00:14:20,595
I'll kick your ass.

192
00:14:20,635 --> 00:14:22,388
I'll fuck up your head!

193
00:14:22,512 --> 00:14:23,598
Let him go!

194
00:14:23,638 --> 00:14:25,183
Mind your own business!

195
00:14:25,307 --> 00:14:26,690
It is my business.

196
00:14:26,725 --> 00:14:28,143
What's the problem?

197
00:14:28,642 --> 00:14:31,062
He said something I didn't like.

198
00:14:31,353 --> 00:14:34,858
About what a girl in a nurse's uniform would
taste like.

199
00:14:35,733 --> 00:14:37,320
Hey, hey, let go of me!

200
00:14:37,611 --> 00:14:38,988
Let go!

201
00:14:39,821 --> 00:14:41,407
Fuck you, Frankenstein!

202
00:14:41,448 --> 00:14:43,074
That's enough. Stop it.

203
00:14:43,449 --> 00:14:45,870
- Ike, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

204
00:14:48,914 --> 00:14:50,124
Everything's fine.

205
00:15:51,099 --> 00:15:52,726
What are you doing?

206
00:15:57,688 --> 00:15:58,982
Come here.

207
00:16:02,318 --> 00:16:03,821
What's the problem?

208
00:16:03,862 --> 00:16:05,698
It's just a stupid mouse.

209
00:16:08,575 --> 00:16:09,869
Got a light?

210
00:16:09,951 --> 00:16:11,786
You know smoking isn't allowed in here...

211
00:16:14,079 --> 00:16:16,458
I have special permission.

212
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:18,502
True story.

213
00:16:18,543 --> 00:16:20,463
Ask Dr. Lang.

214
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:21,505
I will.

215
00:16:21,546 --> 00:16:23,507
He'll tell you it helps me.

216
00:16:24,591 --> 00:16:27,217
With my anxiety.

217
00:16:30,470 --> 00:16:32,014
The truth is...

218
00:16:33,055 --> 00:16:35,185
...it's because I'm his favorite.

219
00:16:35,559 --> 00:16:37,021
He told me so.

220
00:16:37,228 --> 00:16:39,898
- You've earned yourself a warning.
- Why?

221
00:16:39,938 --> 00:16:41,483
I was just taking a bath.

222
00:16:41,523 --> 00:16:42,859
Get out.

223
00:16:46,278 --> 00:16:47,572
Bitch.

224
00:16:49,406 --> 00:16:51,160
Is everything all right?

225
00:16:51,868 --> 00:16:54,079
Yes, Doctor, I'm fine.

226
00:16:54,661 --> 00:16:59,542
I'll handle Isaac and Bud.

227
00:16:59,625 --> 00:17:01,377
No. Bud didn't do anything.

228
00:17:01,418 --> 00:17:03,817
I look forward to our session tomorrow, Jackson.

229
00:17:03,852 --> 00:17:06,216
I'm sorry, but he's actually right.

230
00:17:06,256 --> 00:17:07,551
Bud didn't do anything.

231
00:17:07,592 --> 00:17:09,718
He was fighting...

232
00:17:10,343 --> 00:17:12,012
Well, he was protecting me...

233
00:17:12,094 --> 00:17:13,347
Remind me to tell you later what...

234
00:17:13,387 --> 00:17:14,973
...he did to his last foster family.

235
00:17:15,056 --> 00:17:16,725
Well, they took his dog away.

236
00:17:17,266 --> 00:17:20,562
Yes... that's a perfectly good reason...

237
00:17:20,603 --> 00:17:23,232
...to put someone in a coma.

238
00:17:23,607 --> 00:17:25,108
Well, I'm just saying.

239
00:17:47,546 --> 00:17:48,464
<i>DIAGNOSIS: BIPOLAR DISORDER

240
00:17:48,505 --> 00:17:52,426
<i>Upon admission, this 16-year-old boy,
Horton, Bud, was depressed, agitated and
fearful.

241
00:17:52,551 --> 00:17:55,594
<i>Overall, his behavior was aggressive,
unusually energetic and withdrawn.

242
00:17:58,806 --> 00:18:00,642
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

243
00:18:01,392 --> 00:18:02,727
You didn't.

244
00:18:03,477 --> 00:18:05,063
Thank you for helping Bud.

245
00:18:06,147 --> 00:18:09,775
I know you don't even know him, so that was nice.

246
00:18:10,525 --> 00:18:13,445
Well, I'm here to help you all. So...

247
00:18:15,197 --> 00:18:17,492
You're the first pretty nurse we've had around
here.

248
00:18:20,369 --> 00:18:21,955
So I thought you should know...

249
00:18:23,456 --> 00:18:24,624
Know what?

250
00:18:24,957 --> 00:18:27,587
What goes on in the relaxation room...

251
00:18:28,503 --> 00:18:30,382
The kids around here call it...

252
00:18:30,548 --> 00:18:32,801
...Dr. Lang's chamber of horrors.

253
00:18:33,217 --> 00:18:34,803
Piece of shit.

254
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:36,638
Why is that?

255
00:18:37,013 --> 00:18:39,514
Go there at night and find out for yourself...

256
00:18:41,056 --> 00:18:43,560
Hey, you might even do something about it.

257
00:18:44,935 --> 00:18:46,021
You know.

258
00:18:47,189 --> 00:18:48,316
Jackson...

259
00:18:50,609 --> 00:18:52,777
You'll get out of here one day.

260
00:18:53,068 --> 00:18:55,697
And just because you can't trust certain people...

261
00:18:57,198 --> 00:18:59,326
...doesn't mean you shouldn't trust others.

262
00:19:00,409 --> 00:19:02,037
Well, I'll think about it.

263
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:08,919
<i>DR. LANG

264
00:19:13,506 --> 00:19:15,008
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

265
00:19:15,090 --> 00:19:17,761
Barry Farnsworth, we had an appointment an
hour ago.

266
00:19:17,843 --> 00:19:19,262
Did we?

267
00:19:21,556 --> 00:19:23,098
Mrs. Sawyer.

268
00:19:23,264 --> 00:19:25,434
It's Mrs. Carson now.

269
00:19:31,523 --> 00:19:33,108
I want to see Jed.

270
00:19:33,441 --> 00:19:35,528
We've been through this before.

271
00:19:36,027 --> 00:19:37,404
Year after year...

272
00:19:37,445 --> 00:19:38,781
He's my son.

273
00:19:39,197 --> 00:19:40,825
And I can afford a lawyer now.

274
00:19:40,865 --> 00:19:42,868
That doesn't change anything.

